      "dependency/toolchain/runtime/native/embedded change needs a new binary; S5 keeps the listening socket and transfers state unchanged (state schema identical)",
      "goroutine-structure, long-running or start-up code changed: in-process patching would leave old code running in goroutines that never return; a new process starts the new goroutine structure, and the old one is drained and exits",
      "S6 blockers (32): github.com/cespare/xxhash/v2: dependency graph changed; github.com/go-jose/go-jose/v4: dependency graph changed; github.com/go-logr/logr: dependency graph changed; github.com/go-logr/stdr: dependency graph changed; github.com/google/uuid: dependency graph changed; ... and 27 more"
    ],
    "alternatives": [
      "Kubernetes rolling update (loses in-memory state, needs surge capacity)"
    ],
    "risks": [
      "github.com/gotify/server/v2/auth.Auth.Optional is exported: callers outside the analysed module are not in the closure",
      "github.com/gotify/server/v2/auth.Auth.RequireAdmin is exported: callers outside the analysed module are not in the closure",
      "github.com/gotify/server/v2/auth.Auth.RequireApplicationToken is exported: callers outside the analysed module are not in the closure",
      "github.com/gotify/server/v2/auth.Auth.RequireClient is exported: callers outside the analysed module are not in the closure",
      "github.com/gotify/server/v2/ui.Register is exported: callers outside the analysed module are not in the closure",
      "no patched function has a context.Context parameter: S6 gives per-call (not per-request) consistency, so one request may mix old and new versions of the 32 functions",
      "type information is partial (240/286 type errors old/new; third-party packages are opaque): call-graph and state reachability are lower bounds",
      "quiescence: old activations of main(), init-started or long-running goroutines never return, so the old process is retired by exit, not by draining; set a drain deadline in the S5 upgrader"
    ]
  },
